## 11. Testing and validation
11.1. AI accuracy — test with unseen fish photos; check both detection quality (does YOLO find the fish?) and classification quality (does the CNN name it correctly?) separately — a failure in one stage looks different from a failure in the other, and you'll want to know which one to retrain
11.2. Offline integrity — airplane mode: confirm camera capture, full two-stage inference, species library, and restricted-area/closed-season checks all still work with zero connectivity. This last one is the check that would have caught the earlier contradiction.
11.3. Geofencing correctness — with cached boundary data already on the device, simulate coordinates inside a restricted area, in airplane mode, and confirm the alert still fires
11.4. Scraper test — trigger `GovernmentDataSource.getUpdates()` manually, confirm BFAR data populates `RestrictedArea` correctly
11.5. Sync queue — scan offline, reconnect, confirm `WorkManager` uploads without duplicating records
11.6. Track every bug in GitHub Issues
---

## 12. Refinement
12.1. If YOLO and CNN confuse the same pair of species repeatedly, check which stage is actually failing before adding more data blindly — more detection data won't fix a classification confusion, and vice versa
12.2. Profile combined CPU/memory usage of running two models back-to-back on a budget device using Android Studio Profiler — this is a heavier ask than a single model, so measure it early rather than assuming it'll fit
---


